{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1451636-blood-rage-and-torpor-sleep","id":1451636,"title":"Blood Rage and Torpor/Sleep","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-11T04:49:21-07:00","id":1451636,"title":"Blood Rage and Torpor/Sleep","content":"So, if you use this power, can you force someone to wake prematurely, skipping the lengthly Humanity mandated torpor time for combat wounds/voluntary torpor?<br /> The same may be said for other healing powers like Valeren. <br /> <br /> I am completely uninterested in LARP rules. Please just talk VTM 1e,2e,R or v20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T01:28:36-07:00","id":1451815,"title":"","content":"I don't mean to sound so harsh. Just, when I googled it, a good chunk of answers concerning Torpor were LARP based or a storyteller being very generous with house rules, and I could find nothing specific on using these powers. I'm interested in people's interpretations of what's written, or what they think the authors want/aught to say, not whatever house rule is thrown in to make the game as easy and smooth as possible. I was writing some stuff for storyteller's vault and felt this needed to be clarified one-way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T03:57:22-07:00","id":1451826,"title":"","content":"going by the V20 rulebook: i'd argue no, the book specifies you can exceed the generational bp per turn limit which to me says you can spend bp faster then usual while the humanity time limit isn't about the speed at which you spend bp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T11:22:08-07:00","id":1451882,"title":"","content":"I've always allowed it in games I've run. I felt there should be a method to shorten torpor times because if you're running a story that takes place over a week, saying &quot;Oh sorry June, because of all that damage you took, you can't play your character for a month. Guess you might as well not show up for the next few sessions&quot; seems lame. That having been said, there are some issues to consider. 1) do they have enough blood in their bodies to heal the damage? 2) will they have blood left when you're done. 3) how likely are they to frenzy when they wake up?<br /> <br /> Also, the rules have implied over the years (though never outright stated) that if you force a vampire to spend blood they do not have (ie, they are 0), they take a level of damage for each blood point so spent. So you could even do more harm than good. And that's not even getting into the fact that you'd need 5 successes to force someone to heal a level of aggravated damage and what if you spend 4? If you're feeling unkind, you can say &quot;well, you force them to spend 4 blood points. The power doesn't say you can use a lesser effect, so they waste 4 blood for nothing. Sorry.&quot; Now if your Chronicle is one where long torpor times aren't a big deal, or you're a very &quot;torpor/death should matter&quot; kind of Storyteller, of course you can say Blood Rage can't do this. But the power, like so many in Vampire, is open ended and ambiguously written, so I feel forcing someone to heal is a valid use of the ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T13:58:59-07:00","id":1451902,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25992\" data-vbnamecard=\"25992\">archderd</a> it seems to me that the real crux of it is that the wording is very much &quot;if you enter torpor through combat then you can't do anything for an amount of time&quot; which suggests if someone tried to blood rage you to full health and then wake you up you'd still not be able to do anything and essentially remain in slumber. Though some parts suggest -<i>you specifically- </i>can't try to wake till the time has passed. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24241_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24241\" data-vbnamecard=\"24241\">Lynceus</a> Torpored Vampires ingest blood they are fed without conscious effort. Infact, if you enter Torpor by starvation (IE burning through blood and health) you're sleeping until someone feeds you blood; You'll wake up regardless of your humanity. Which makes me imagine critically injured vampires trying to force themselves to Torpor themselves the right way so that they'll lose agro and their friends can bring them back right after the conflict. if starvation is so easy, I'm not really sure why combat or voluntary torpor wouldn't end once the wounds heal and there's blood in you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T23:38:36-07:00","id":1451953,"title":"","content":"That's a fair point, in my games you can voluntarily enter torpor to heal faster, which a lot of characters opt to do when they take a lot of aggravated damage. But it was nice to have a backup option and this was the only one that is at least technically legal that I know of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-13T00:39:41-07:00","id":1451958,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of making things work as close to movies and novels I like, so I houserule it so that feeding someone a full human life heals an agg, and brings vampires out of torpor. The RAW is just too far from how it works in movies/novels for my tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:44:28-07:00","id":1452463,"title":"","content":"From my perspective, it's the 'can't spend blood' of torpor, versus the 'forced to spend blood' of blood rage. In my games, the 'can't' wins out. It's the same for being staked. Of course, I have other house rules to get players out of torpor more quickly, because again, why say to a player - 'don't bother showing up until the other, notoriously slow to progress, PCs have managed to get through a month of game time.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T08:22:32-07:00","id":1452482,"title":"","content":"No. If a character enters voluntary torpor or falls into it via damage, they're down for the whole count -- sparing the smattering of discipline powers that can prematurely awaken a vampire from torpor. If another vampire were to blood rage them to heal, they'd clear health levels but remain in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}